    "created_at": "2023-08-24T18:01:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-08-24T18:01:48Z",
    "body": "I think you're right. The execution context stack just consists of the realm execution context, and nothing else.\r\n\r\nThis was added in https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/12cdfefad607fc824e6ea64a4b967fc24043f684. It seems the issue was discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3117 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3163 was supposed to fix it, but only fixed it for something like `Promise.resolve().then(setTimeout.bind(...))` and not for `setTimeout(setTimeout.bind(...))`?\r\n\r\nSo yeah, we should probably account for cases like this, similar to the defaulting we do in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hostloadimportedmodule .",
